# Shiny your Research 

## Shiny fundamentals

- **Shiny official website**: <https://shiny.posit.co/>

- **Mastering Shiny** — Free online book by Hadley Wickham for deeper learning after the workshop.  
  <https://mastering-shiny.org/>

- **bslib** — Tools for modern Shiny layouts, themes, cards, sidebars, and dashboards.  
  <https://rstudio.github.io/bslib/>  

## Interactive Output

- **DT** — Interactive tables <https://rstudio.github.io/DT/>

- **reactable** - Interactive tables <https://glin.github.io/reactable/>

- **plotly** - Interactive plots: <https://plotly.com/r/>

- **timevis** - Interactive timeline visualizations: <https://github.com/daattali/timevis>

- **leaflet** — Interactive maps: <https://rstudio.github.io/leaflet/>

## Modules and scaling apps

- **Shiny modules** — Official guide to using modules for reusable Shiny components: 
  <https://shiny.posit.co/r/articles/improve/modules/>

- **Engineering Production-Grade Shiny Apps** — Free online book on structuring, scaling, and maintaining Shiny apps: 
  <https://engineering-shiny.org/>

- **golem**: Framework for building production-grade apps: <https://thinkr-open.github.io/golem/>

- **rhino**: Enterprise-level software engineering: <https://appsilon.github.io/rhino/>


## Deployment and sharing

- **Official deployment guides**: <https://shiny.posit.co/r/deploy.html>

- **shinyapps.io** — Hosted deployment option for sharing Shiny apps online.  
  <https://www.shinyapps.io/>


## AI-assisted Shiny exploration

- **ellmer** — The R package for working with large language models from R: <https://ellmer.tidyverse.org/>

- **shinychat** - plug-and-play user interface (UI): <https://posit-dev.github.io/shinychat/>

- **ragnar** - Implementing Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) workflows in R: <https://ragnar.tidyverse.org/>

- **querychat** — Tools for adding natural-language data exploration to Shiny apps:  
  <https://posit-dev.github.io/querychat/>


